.Dd August 17, 2026
.Dt WIFI-TUI 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm wifi-tui
.Nd interactive terminal Wi-Fi controller
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a full-screen
.Xr ncurses 3
front end for NetworkManager.
It lists nearby access points, connects to open and secured networks, handles
hidden and custom SSIDs, and shows the current IPv4 address, netmask, default
gateway and DNS servers.
.Pp
This is the Linux build, written for Debian 13 and any other system where
NetworkManager manages the wireless device.
All state is read and changed through
.Xr nmcli 1 ;
.Nm
never talks to the kernel or to
.Xr wpa_supplicant 8
directly.
A FreeBSD build that drives
.Xr wpa_cli 8
and
.Xr ifconfig 8
instead lives in the
.Pa FreeBSD
subdirectory of the source tree.
.Pp
The wireless interface is chosen automatically: the first NetworkManager
device of type
.Dq wifi
that is connected wins, otherwise the first one present.
.Ss Keys
.Bl -tag -width "Home / End, PgUp / PgDn" -offset indent
.It Ic Up No / Ic Down
Select a network.
.It Ic Left No / Ic Right
Move the focus between the network list and the status panel.
.It Ic Enter
Connect to the selected network.
.It Ic a
Add or connect to a custom or hidden SSID.
.It Ic r
Rescan for nearby networks.
.It Ic d
Disconnect the wireless interface.
.It Ic Home No / Ic End , Ic PgUp No / Ic PgDn
Move through a long list.
.It Ic q
Quit.
.El
.Ss Connecting
.Nm
first tries to activate the network without supplying credentials, which
succeeds when NetworkManager already has a saved profile for it.
Only if that fails does it prompt for a password and retry.
The password is written to
.Xr nmcli 1
on standard input rather than passed as an argument, so it does not appear in
.Xr ps 1
output.
.Pp
WPA Enterprise
.Pq 802.1X
networks are detected and refused.
Configure them first with
.Xr nmtui 1
or
.Nm nm-connection-editor ;
once a profile exists,
.Nm
activates it like any other.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
Check that NetworkManager owns the wireless device before starting:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
nmcli device status
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr nmcli 1 ,
.Xr nmtui 1 ,
.Xr NetworkManager 8
.Sh AUTHORS
.An HIRECHE BAGHDAD BELKHEIR
.Sh CAVEATS
Run
.Nm
as your ordinary desktop user.
NetworkManager and Polkit may ask for authorization depending on system
policy; running the whole program under
.Xr sudo 8
just to connect to Wi-Fi is neither necessary nor advisable.
.Pp
Only IPv4 addressing is displayed.
